    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "e37251cf_712fe511",
        "filename": "microdroid/init.rc",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 33,
      "author": {
        "id": 1415877
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-09-07T01:44:02Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Can we re-use \u0027apexd.status\u003dready\u0027 which tells we can use contents from apexes? In a normal Android, this is set by \u0027apexd --snapshotde\u0027, which is not run in vm mode.\n\nFor now, apexd --vm sets apexd.status\u003dready[1], but it seems to be right for init to set it after running \u0027perform_apex_config\u0027, not by \u0027apexd --vm\u0027\n\n[1] https://cs.android.com/android/platform/superproject/+/master:system/apex/apexd/apexd.cpp;l\u003d3396-3398?q\u003dapexd.cpp",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 33,
        "startChar": 12,
        "endLine": 33,
        "endChar": 30
      },
      "revId": "428a96f871b4dba8603d40c9c9be67e8aac7e56e",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "7e5773d5_fb39f563",
        "filename": "microdroid/init.rc",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 33,
      "author": {
        "id": 1132673
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-09-07T05:15:21Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "apexd.status has been set by apexd. I don\u0027t think it\u0027s good to make an exception to that just to not introduce a new sysprop.",
      "parentUuid": "e37251cf_712fe511",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 33,
        "startChar": 12,
        "endLine": 33,
        "endChar": 30
      },
      "revId": "428a96f871b4dba8603d40c9c9be67e8aac7e56e",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "20cfbd08_b3b4ecda",
        "filename": "microdroid/init.rc",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 33,
      "author": {
        "id": 1415877
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-09-07T05:31:39Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "IMO it would fix the current/wrong behavior of apexd setting apexd.status\u003dready even when APEXes are not ready to be used yet.",
      "parentUuid": "7e5773d5_fb39f563",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 33,
        "startChar": 12,
        "endLine": 33,
        "endChar": 30
      },
      "revId": "428a96f871b4dba8603d40c9c9be67e8aac7e56e",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "3338ea0b_238643e8",
        "filename": "microdroid/init.rc",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 33,
      "author": {
        "id": 1132673
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-09-07T05:44:51Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The meaning of apexd.status\u003dready has been clear. It means that APEXes are correctly mounted and can be accessed via the /apex paths [1]. Therefore, I don\u0027t think the current behavior is wrong. It does not mean that the extra steps like linkerconfig, etc. are done. Those steps themselves could be triggered from apexd.status\u003dready.\n\nIf someone wants to wait until the linkerconfig becomes ready, they should wait for the sysprop for the very event, not an event from apexd which might be an impl detail of linkerconfig.\n\n[1] https://cs.android.com/android/platform/superproject/+/master:system/apex/apexd/apexd.cpp;drc\u003dmaster;l\u003d2945",
      "parentUuid": "20cfbd08_b3b4ecda",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 33,
        "startChar": 12,
        "endLine": 33,
        "endChar": 30
      },
      "revId": "428a96f871b4dba8603d40c9c9be67e8aac7e56e",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "b1b23fe0_6c380d13",
        "filename": "microdroid/init.rc",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 33,
      "author": {
        "id": 1415877
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-09-07T06:09:33Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e Therefore, I don\u0027t think the current behavior is wrong. It does not mean that the extra steps like linkerconfig, etc. are done. Those steps themselves could be triggered from apexd.status\u003dready.\n\nHmm, this differs from what I understand. AFAIK, apexd.status\u003dready is known as THE event for which other components wanting to use something from APEXes should wait. Yeah, the fact that linkerconfig generates configurations for apexes is the implementation detail, but apexd.status\u003dready should imply that as well. I mean, after apexd.status\u003dready, we should be able to \"use\" /apex even for running a binary in it.\n\nThere\u0027s apexd.status\u003dactivated which tells you can \"read\" contents from /apex, but for most cases, we only need to care about \"\u003dready\".",
      "parentUuid": "3338ea0b_238643e8",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 33,
        "startChar": 12,
        "endLine": 33,
        "endChar": 30
      },
      "revId": "428a96f871b4dba8603d40c9c9be67e8aac7e56e",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "a95f0f13_88e3a4a7",
        "filename": "microdroid/init.rc",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 33,
      "author": {
        "id": 1132673
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-09-07T06:30:57Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "That doesn\u0027t match with the documentation [1]\n\n`perform_apex_config`\n Performs tasks after APEXes are mounted. For example, creates data directories\n  for the mounted APEXes, parses config file(s) from them, and updates linker\n  configurations. Intended to be used only once when apexd notifies the mount\n  event by setting `apexd.status` to ready.\n  \nThe document might be outdated. I think that the definition of apexd.status has evolved quite a bit but the interpretation of the sysprop seems to be differ in many places.\n  \nIf you think apexd.status\u003dready should imply linkerconfig as well, please file a new bug to make it consistent throughout Android. That change shall include the removal of linkerconfig.ready property that I am adding here. I think that is out of scope of this CL.\n  \n[1] https://source.corp.google.com/android/system/core/init/README.md;rcl\u003d3d532080727a79dbba23fed5a97adb56fe7e5ae2;l\u003d610",
      "parentUuid": "b1b23fe0_6c380d13",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 33,
        "startChar": 12,
        "endLine": 33,
        "endChar": 30
      },
      "revId": "428a96f871b4dba8603d40c9c9be67e8aac7e56e",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "84a8cab3_1a790057",
        "filename": "microdroid/init.rc",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 33,
      "author": {
        "id": 1415877
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-09-07T07:46:54Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Ack. Then, can you rename the property for now? Setting \u0027linkerconfig.ready` here is hard to follow. It\u0027s highly coupled with what `perform_apex_config` does but it\u0027s not that straightforward. At least it looks like it should be linkerconfig itself to set the prop. I don\u0027t have a good idea about naming, but what about \"apex_config.done\"?",
      "parentUuid": "a95f0f13_88e3a4a7",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 33,
        "startChar": 12,
        "endLine": 33,
        "endChar": 30
      },
      "revId": "428a96f871b4dba8603d40c9c9be67e8aac7e56e",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
